From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] xilinx: skip null net entries while packing constants

Yosys JSON re-emission can leave erased net slots in the context map. The
Xilinx constant packer currently dereferences those entries unconditionally,
causing a deterministic SIGSEGV before placement. Ignore null slots; they do
not represent a live net and cannot carry a constant driver.

--- a/xilinx/pack.cc
+++ b/xilinx/pack.cc
@@
     for (auto net : sorted(ctx->nets)) {
         NetInfo *ni = net.second;
+        if (ni == nullptr)
+            continue;
         if (ni->driver.cell != nullptr && ni->driver.cell->type == ctx->id("GND")) {
